[32m+[m[32m# Analysis[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Approach[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe solution uses a sweep-line algorithm based on booking start and end events.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEach booking is represented by two events:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* `(start, +1)` when a booking starts.[m
[32m+[m[32m* `(end, -1)` when a booking ends.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll events are then sorted by timestamp. The algorithm processes the sorted events from left to right while maintaining the current room occupancy.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen the current occupancy becomes greater than the maximum occupancy found so far, a new peak interval starts. When the occupancy drops below the current maximum, the peak interval ends at that timestamp.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis approach avoids comparing every booking against every other booking.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2. Algorithm[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFor example, given:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32m(9, 12)[m
[32m+[m[32m(10, 13)[m
[32m+[m[32m(11, 14)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mthe bookings are converted into:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32m9  -> +1[m
[32m+[m[32m10 -> +1[m
[32m+[m[32m11 -> +1[m
[32m+[m[32m12 -> -1[m
[32m+[m[32m13 -> -1[m
[32m+[m[32m14 -> -1[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAfter sorting, the algorithm performs a single sweep:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mTime    Change    Occupancy[m
[32m+[m[32m9       +1        1[m
[32m+[m[32m10      +1        2[m
[32m+[m[32m11      +1        3[m
[32m+[m[32m12      -1        2[m
[32m+[m[32m13      -1        1[m
[32m+[m[32m14      -1        0[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe maximum occupancy is `3`, and it occurs from `11` to `12`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe returned result is therefore:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```python[m
[32m+[m[32m(3, 11, 12)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Simultaneous start and end events[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe implementation uses Python tuple ordering when sorting events.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFor events occurring at the same timestamp:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```python[m
[32m+[m[32m(12, -1)[m
[32m+[m[32m(12, +1)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mthe end event is processed before the start event because `-1 < +1`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis matches the interval semantics used by the examples: bookings are treated as half-open intervals `[start, end)`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTherefore, a booking ending at time `T` is no longer active at `T`, while another booking starting at `T` becomes active at `T`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFor example:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```python[m
[32m+[m[32m[(9, 10), (10, 11)][m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mhas a maximum occupancy of `1`, not `2`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 3. Complexity[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mLet `n` be the number of bookings.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEach booking produces two events, resulting in `2n` events.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Time complexity[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* Creating the events: `O(n)`[m
[32m+[m[32m* Sorting the events: `O(n log n)`[m
[32m+[m[32m* Sweeping through the events: `O(n)`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTherefore, the overall time complexity is:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mO(n log n)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe sorting step dominates the total running time.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Space complexity[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe algorithm stores two events for every booking.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTherefore, the additional memory required is:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mO(n)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis is necessary because the events must be stored before sorting.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 4. Why This Approach Scales[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA naive pairwise approach could compare every booking with every other booking, resulting in `O(n²)` time complexity.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFor hundreds of thousands of bookings, that approach would require an impractical number of comparisons.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe event-based approach reduces the problem to sorting the event timestamps and performing a linear sweep afterward.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIts `O(n log n)` time complexity makes it substantially more suitable for large input volumes.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 5. Edge Cases[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe test suite covers the following cases:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* Empty booking list.[m
[32m+[m[32m* A single booking.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Multiple overlapping bookings.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Completely non-overlapping bookings.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Multiple bookings starting at the same time.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Multiple bookings ending at the same time.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Bookings ending and starting at the same timestamp.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Identical bookings.[m
[32m+[m[32m* A peak that starts after an initial booking.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Multiple separate peak intervals with the same maximum occupancy.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Multiple endings and starts occurring at the same timestamp.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe implementation was validated with all official examples and the additional edge cases above.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 6. Assumptions and Unspecified Behavior[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Interval semantics[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBookings are treated as half-open intervals:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32m[start, end)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis means the start time is included and the end time is excluded.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis behavior is consistent with the provided example where:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```python[m
[32m+[m[32m[(9, 10), (10, 11), (11, 12)][m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mreturns:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```python[m
[32m+[m[32m(1, 9, 10)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mrather than considering the bookings overlapping at their boundaries.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Multiple maximum occupancy periods[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe problem statement does not specify what should happen if multiple separate time intervals have the same maximum occupancy.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe implementation deterministically returns the first maximum-occupancy interval in chronological order.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFor example:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```python[m
[32m+[m[32m[(9, 11), (10, 11), (14, 16), (15, 16)][m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mreturns:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```python[m
[32m+[m[32m(2, 10, 11)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Invalid intervals[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe implementation assumes that bookings are valid intervals where:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mstart < end[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe problem statement does not define behavior for invalid bookings, so invalid intervals are considered outside the function's input contract.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m7. Testing[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe implementation is tested with pytest.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe current test suite contains 11 tests covering the official examples, normal scenarios, boundary conditions, and edge cases.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAt the time of writing, all 11 tests pass.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDuring development, testing also identified a case where separate peak intervals with the same occupancy could incorrectly be merged into a single interval. The implementation was adjusted so that once a peak interval has ended, a later interval with the same occupancy is treated as a separate peak.[m
